-- CONSIDERs with a WHEN that is not one yes-or-no condition: a pattern that
-- names the fields of an option, a pattern inside a pattern, a new name that
-- matches anything, and an OTHERWISE before the last WHEN. None of these
-- rules answers TRUE or FALSE, so none of them is covered, and the report
-- must say so and say why, not count them as rules with no condition to
-- branch on (smucclaw/l4-ide#1094).
DECLARE Plan IS ONE OF basic, pro, team
DECLARE Seats IS ONE OF single, many HAS count IS A NUMBER

GIVEN s IS A Seats
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee by seats` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN single THEN 5
    WHEN many n THEN n TIMES 4

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee if any` m IS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST basic THEN 5
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN p IS A Plan
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee with a new name` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN basic THEN 5
    WHEN other THEN 50

GIVEN p IS A Plan
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fee with an early OTHERWISE` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN basic THEN 5
    OTHERWISE 50
    WHEN pro THEN 20
